.git
.github
.superpowers
# docs/ is excluded wholesale -- security findings and design specs have no
# business in a running container -- EXCEPT the manual, which the app serves
# at /manual and therefore has to be able to read at runtime. See
# app/services/manual/source.rb, which raises pointing back at this file.
docs
!docs/manual
# The GitHub Pages build. docs-site/build/ and docs-site/site/ are gitignored,
# so `git status` never shows them and they are absent from CI's fresh
# checkout -- but they are ~4.8 MB of staged markdown and rendered HTML in a
# local build context, and the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`. Anyone who previews
# the site and then runs `kamal deploy` from their laptop bakes them into the
# production image. Same machine-seam class as the libvips package names and
# the !docs/manual line above: master looks clean because CI never has these
# directories to ship. (bin/stage-docs-site stays -- bin/ is copied wholesale
# -- and would raise LoadError if anyone ran it inside the container. Nothing
# does: the site is built in CI, from a checkout.)
docs-site
features
spec
tmp
log
node_modules
db/*.sqlite3
db/*.sqlite
.env*
ansible
